Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: use the real pixel rate for the link bandwidth check

msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid() halves the pixel clock when wide bus is
available, which is right for the DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ limit (two pixels
per controller clock), and then reuses the halved clock for bpp selection
and the link bandwidth check. Wide bus does not halve the data on the link
(only YUV 4:2:0 does), so modes needing up to twice the link budget are
accepted.

Seen on a OnePlus 7 Pro (2 DP lanes, HBR2 = 8.64 Gb/s) with a 3440x1440
monitor: the 100 Hz mode (543.5 MHz, >= 9.8 Gb/s even at 18 bpp) passed
mode_valid, was set, link-trained, and the monitor stayed black. The 60 Hz
mode (319.75 MHz, 7.67 Gb/s at 24 bpp) works.

Keep the halved clock for the pixel clock limit and use the link pixel rate
(halved only for 4:2:0) for bpp selection and the bandwidth check.
Nura-Category: upstream-fix
Nura-Origin: nura rc4h dock debugging
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2 (wide bus still halves the link rate)
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c	2026-11-13 21:20:53.530924976 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c	2026-11-13 21:20:53.536246204 +0100
@@ -938,6 +938,8 @@
 	u32 mode_rate_khz = 0, supported_rate_khz = 0, mode_bpp = 0;
 	struct msm_dp *dp;
 	int mode_pclk_khz = mode->clock;
+	int link_pclk_khz = mode->clock;
+	bool yuv420;
 
 	dp = to_dp_bridge(bridge)->msm_dp_display;
 
@@ -949,10 +951,20 @@
 	msm_dp_display = container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 	link_info = &msm_dp_display->panel->link_info;
 
-	if ((drm_mode_is_420_only(&dp->connector->display_info, mode) &&
-	     msm_dp_display->panel->vsc_sdp_supported) ||
-	     msm_dp_wide_bus_available(dp))
+	yuv420 = drm_mode_is_420_only(&dp->connector->display_info, mode) &&
+		 msm_dp_display->panel->vsc_sdp_supported;
+
+	/*
+	 * Wide bus moves two pixels per controller clock, so it halves the
+	 * clock that must stay under DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ. It does not halve
+	 * the data on the link; only YUV 4:2:0 does. Using the halved clock
+	 * for the bandwidth check below accepted modes twice the link budget
+	 * (3440x1440@100, 543.5 MHz, on HBR2 x2 lanes) and lit a black sink.
+	 */
+	if (yuv420 || msm_dp_wide_bus_available(dp))
 		mode_pclk_khz /= 2;
+	if (yuv420)
+		link_pclk_khz /= 2;
 
 	if (mode_pclk_khz > DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ)
 		return MODE_CLOCK_HIGH;
@@ -962,9 +974,9 @@
 		mode_bpp = default_bpp;
 
 	mode_bpp = msm_dp_panel_get_mode_bpp(msm_dp_display->panel,
-			mode_bpp, mode_pclk_khz);
+			mode_bpp, link_pclk_khz);
 
-	mode_rate_khz = mode_pclk_khz * mode_bpp;
+	mode_rate_khz = link_pclk_khz * mode_bpp;
 	supported_rate_khz = link_info->num_lanes * link_info->rate * 8;
 
 	if (mode_rate_khz > supported_rate_khz)
